\par \cell {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\s16\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\sl360\slmult1
\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls1\adjustright\rin0\lin720\pararsid11022883\yts15\contextualspace \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 Exotic breeds or their crossbreeds are known for high milk production. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\s16\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\sl360\slmult1
\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls3\adjustright\rin0\lin720\pararsid11022883\yts15\contextualspace {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 
Holstein Friesian: Black and white or red and white, no hump. With good management, they can yield 30 liters of milk per day and can be milked for 10 consecutive months. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Jersey: Brown or black with white spots, prominent eyes. They yield over 20 liters per day and can be milked for 10 consecutive months. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Crossb}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid920297\charrsid11022883 reeds:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883  Cows resulting from crossing exotic breeds with local breeds can yield 8\endash 10 liters per day and be milked for 10 consecutive months. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
If exotic or crossbred cows/heifers are unavailable, select local breeds known for better milk production in the area. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Selection by Physical Conformation: Choose cows with a triangular body shape (narrower at the neck, wider at the flanks), wide belly, wide spacing between ribs, long legs, and a large, well-attached udder with large teats. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}When selecting local breeds for improvement, consider good stature, health status, and age. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Selecting Bulls: Choose bulls that are free from reproductive diseases, have long straight legs, two visible testicles, are neither too fat nor too thin, and are up to five years old. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid7431811\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
If the area has a raw milk market, balanced feed, and health services, Holstein Friesian crossbreeds are appropriate for their high yield. If the area is hot and raw milk markets are inconvenient, Jersey crossbreeds are better as their milk has higher fat
 content, suitable for processing and selling as butter. 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\sl360\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\pararsid11022883\yts15 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 
