\f0\fs24\insrsid15092560\charrsid11022883 It is a highly contagious and economically devastating disease that affects cloven-hoofed animals, causing lesions in the mouth, on the feet, and on the udder and teats, leading to severe drops in productivity.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 Transmission:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
The virus spreads through aerosols (airborne transmission), contaminated fomites (objects like equipment, vehicles, and clothing), feed, water, and people. It is also shed in all excretions and secretions, including milk, saliva, urine, feces, and semen, 
facilitating both direct and indirect contact transmission.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 Zoonotic Note}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
: While extremely rare, the virus can infect humans; however, it does not cause significant illness. Strict biosecurity and hygiene measures are essential for handlers to prevent mechanical spread.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 Symptoms:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
The primary symptom is the appearance of vesicles (fluid-filled blisters) on the tongue, gums, dental pad, lips, coronary bands of the hooves, and teats. Immediately upon suspicion, isolate the animal and contact veterinary authorities. Subsequent signs i
nclude ruptured vesicles forming painful erosions and ulcers, severe lameness, profuse salivation, nasal discharge, fever, anorexia, and a drastic drop in milk yield ("milk drop syndrome"). Pregnant animals may abort.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \li360\ri0\sl360\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\pararsid11022883\yts15 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f31506\fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 Treatment and Care}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid4483265\charrsid11022883 : }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
There is no specific antiviral treatment for FMD. Veterinary care is supportive and palliative, aimed at preventing secondary bacterial infections in the lesions, managing pain, and maintaining hydration and nutrition. Any suspected case must be reported 
to government veterinary services immediately.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\sl360\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\pararsid11022883\yts15 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 \bullet  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 Supportive Home Care}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
: Isolate affected animals. Gently clean mouth and foot lesions with a mild antiseptic solution (e.g., diluted potassium permanganate). Applying emollients like honey or glycerin can aid healing and provide a protective barrier. Provide soft, palatable fe
ed and easy access to clean water.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid1058738\charrsid11022883 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 \bullet  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 Prevention}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9772787\charrsid11022883 
: Vaccination is a key control measure in endemic regions. The cornerstone of prevention is strict biosecurity: controlling animal movement, disinfecting equipment and premises, and maintaining a quarantine period for new animals.\cell 
}\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\intbl\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f31506\fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
