ize income and reduces market price volatility.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 Transportation & Quality:}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 
 Transport milk in clean, food-grade stainless steel or aluminum containers that are light-proof (e.g., milk churns, "Mazican"). Containers should have wide openings for thorough cleaning and inspection. Adulteration (adding water or foreign substances) i
s strictly prohibited as it compromises public health and severely downgrades quality. Maintain milk quality by keeping it clean, covered, and cooled immediately after milking to ensure a premium price.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Surplus Sales (Livestock & Feed): Sell surplus heifers at optimal market prices. Cull and sell older cows with declining production and male calves not intended for breeding to local rearers or feedlot operators. Sell any excess fodder or conserved feed t
o generate additional farm revenue.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid8849958\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid8849958\charrsid11022883 Cost Management: }{\rtlch\fcs1 
