\f31506\fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs24\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 Manure Management}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 
: Improper handling of manure and urine elevates moisture levels and ammonia (NH\u8323\'5f
) concentrations in the barn environment. This compromises air quality, suppresses cattle feed intake (dry matter consumption), and creates ideal breeding sites for flies and
 pathogens (bacteria and viruses). To mitigate this, thoroughly clean the barn daily and scrub feed and water troughs 2\endash 3 times per week to remove organic residue.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
 Nutrient Utilization: Cattle manure is a valuable source of the primary macronutrients Nitrogen (N), Phosphorus (P), and Potassium (K).
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}As Fertilizer: Properly compost and store manure to produce stable organic fertilizer for crop production.

\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
As Energy: Collect manure in an anaerobic digester (biogas plant) to produce methane-rich biogas through fermentation, providing a renewable energy source for cooking or electricity.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
 Carcass Disposal: Animals that die from infectious disease must be removed and disposed of immediately to break the disease transmission cycle and prevent environmental contamination.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s16 \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}
Recommended Methods: Bury carcasses in a deep, secure pit (at least 2 meters deep) located away from water sources, or incinerate them.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \intbl\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\insrsid14774918\charrsid11022883 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \ltrpar\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\sl360\slmult1
